1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,620
Every class ends the same way.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:08,770
The board fills up, the phones come out,
and the photo lands in a camera roll.

3
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:12,706
For many of us, that's
the last time we see it.

4
00:00:12,786 --> 00:00:16,770
It feels like studying,
but nothing has happened yet.

5
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:19,611
alRato keeps the two-second habit.

6
00:00:19,691 --> 00:00:22,017
Snap the board and look back up.

7
00:00:22,097 --> 00:00:26,296
"Al rato" is Latin American
Spanish for "in a little while",

8
00:00:26,376 --> 00:00:28,770
and that's when the work happens.

9
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:32,096
Later, it reads the photo, math included.

10
00:00:32,176 --> 00:00:37,273
Built on Firebase AI Logic, alRato
picks an inference mode for each task.

11
00:00:37,353 --> 00:00:42,450
Reading handwriting prefers the cloud,
so this receipt says In the cloud,

12
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,938
with the bytes sent and the time.

13
00:00:45,018 --> 00:00:48,770
That label is the real
inference source from the SDK.

14
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:51,818
It won't just hand over the answer.

15
00:00:51,898 --> 00:00:56,398
In one large field study,
unguarded AI raised practice scores

16
00:00:56,478 --> 00:00:58,724
and then lowered exam scores.

17
00:00:58,804 --> 00:01:03,233
So alRato gives you a ladder:
a nudge, a hint, a first step,

18
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:05,770
and only then the full solution.

19
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:09,081
Here's the moment we built this for.

20
00:01:09,161 --> 00:01:14,952
This exercise looks new, but you already
have a note on weighted averages,

21
00:01:15,032 --> 00:01:21,501
and alRato finds it, by matching what this
note needs against what your older notes

22
00:01:21,581 --> 00:01:23,910
teach, right on your device.

23
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:26,770
The probabilities are the weights.

24
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:31,845
On a laptop with Gemini Nano,
the same hint runs locally.

25
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:36,073
The receipt now says
On this device, nothing sent.

26
00:01:36,153 --> 00:01:40,770
Same code, same schema,
a different route for this task.

27
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:43,481
Now we cut the network.

28
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:46,250
The laptop keeps answering.

29
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:52,054
The phone has no local model,
so it saves the note and waits.

30
00:01:52,134 --> 00:01:57,770
When the connection comes back,
the note finishes by itself.

31
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:01,709
Some notes should never leave your device.

32
00:02:01,789 --> 00:02:05,982
Mark one private and it runs
locally, or it waits.

33
00:02:06,062 --> 00:02:12,627
We found that the SDK's device-only mode
can reach the cloud in browsers without

34
00:02:12,707 --> 00:02:17,770
the Prompt API, so alRato blocks
that call before it happens.

35
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:20,912
Finally, the note becomes practice.

36
00:02:20,992 --> 00:02:26,086
You try to recall it, check yourself,
and it comes back days later.

37
00:02:26,166 --> 00:02:31,770
Recall and spacing are two of the
best-supported study techniques we have.

38
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:36,219
alRato is open source.

39
00:02:36,299 --> 00:02:38,771
Snap it now.

40
00:02:38,851 --> 00:02:42,920
Understand it al rato.
